2026-05-24 21:38:43.495 [info] [requirements-analyzer] Received item -  {"requirementId":"REQ-16.1","question":"When approving a quarantined email with a linked signal, should the system validate that the linked signal is specifically a CALENDAR type before forwarding, or should it forward regardless of the linked signal's type?","answerChoices":[{"answer":"Validate signal types - only forward if the linked signal is specifically a CALENDAR type","consequence":"The system will only forward .ics files when the linked signal is confirmed to be a calendar type, preventing potential errors from processing non-calendar signals."},{"answer":"Forward regardless - trust that any linked signal can be processed as a calendar invite","consequence":"The system will attempt to forward any linked signal as a calendar invite, which could cause errors if the linked signal is not actually calendar data."}],"defaultChoice":{"answer":"Validate signal types - only forward if the linked signal is specifically a CALENDAR type"},"responseType":"CLARIFYING_QUESTIONS","autoResolvable":true,"recommendedAnswer":"Validate signal types - only forward if the linked signal is specifically a CALENDAR type"}
