2026-05-24 21:39:50.030 [info] [requirements-analyzer] Received item -  {"requirementId":"REQ-1.5","question":"The spec says calendar invites from recruiters should go to the 'job' workflow, but in the case where a recruiter sends a calendar invite that's more about ongoing relationship management than a specific job opportunity, should it still be forced into the job workflow or allowed to go to CRM?","answerChoices":[{"answer":"Always assign recruiter calendar invites to the job workflow as specified","consequence":"Ensures consistent classification based on sender role, but may misclassify relationship-building meetings that aren't about specific job opportunities"},{"answer":"Allow context-sensitive assignment between job and CRM workflows for recruiters","consequence":"Enables more accurate classification of recruiter intent, but requires more complex logic to distinguish job-related vs relationship-building calendar invites"}],"defaultChoice":{"answer":"Always assign recruiter calendar invites to the job workflow as specified"},"responseType":"CLARIFYING_QUESTIONS","autoResolvable":false,"recommendedAnswer":""}
