2026-05-24 21:44:34.825 [info] [requirements-analyzer] Received item -  {"requirementId":"REQ-5.1","question":"When rejecting an oversized .ics attachment, should the system track rejection at both the attachment level and parse result level, or is setting parse_result to REJECTED sufficient?","answerChoices":[{"answer":"Parse result rejection is sufficient","consequence":"The system tracks rejection through parse_result = REJECTED without requiring a separate attachment_rejected flag."},{"answer":"Both attachment and parse result rejection required","consequence":"The system must set both attachment_rejected = true and parse_result = REJECTED to properly track the rejection."}],"defaultChoice":{"answer":"Parse result rejection is sufficient"},"responseType":"CLARIFYING_QUESTIONS","autoResolvable":true,"recommendedAnswer":"Parse result rejection is sufficient"}
2026-05-24 21:44:34.834 [info] [requirements-analyzer] Received item -  {"requirementId":"REQ-5.2","question":"When rejecting an attachment due to a VTIMEZONE bomb, should the system set both the parse_result to REJECTED and the attachment_rejected flag, or is setting parse_result to REJECTED sufficient?","answerChoices":[{"answer":"Set only parse_result to REJECTED","consequence":"The system uses a single rejection mechanism through the parse result status."},{"answer":"Set both attachment_rejected flag and parse_result to REJECTED","consequence":"The system uses dual rejection mechanisms to ensure the attachment is marked as rejected at multiple levels."}],"defaultChoice":{"answer":"Set only parse_result to REJECTED"},"responseType":"CLARIFYING_QUESTIONS","autoResolvable":false,"recommendedAnswer":""}
